{% doc %}
  Outputs 'A' or 'B' based on the product's supplier source. Used by Book Install
  triggers to set data-supplier-tier so the install modal can pick the correct
  lead-time floor.

  Tier B = a supplier's warehouse (next-business-day after 12:30 PM)
    - Tag "Supplier Stock" — checked FIRST and wins over everything below.
      ATW sells the very brands we import, so a Haida or Tesche sitting in
      ATW's Edmonton warehouse must NOT be offered as a two-hour install
      just because of its brand name.
    - Default for everything else (most products tagged "Trail Tire Supply")

  Tier A = in stock at our shop (2 hr lead time)
    - Tag "Prince Stock" (or legacy "Prince Tires")
    - OR collection handle "imported-tires"
    - OR vendor matches one of our imported brands

  Canonical brand list lives here. Add new imported brands by editing tierA_brands below.
  Mirrored server-side in princetires-app/src/app/api/book/route.ts — keep in sync.

  @param {object} product - The Shopify product object

  @example
    {%- capture supplier_tier -%}{% render 'pt-supplier-tier', product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
    <button data-supplier-tier="{{ supplier_tier | strip }}">Book installation</button>
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign tier = 'B'
  assign tierA_brands = 'haida,tesche,composal,suretrac,sierra,bearway' | split: ','

  comment
    Supplier stock is never Tier A, whatever the brand or collection says. The
    tag records where the tire physically IS, which is what a lead time is
    about; the checks below are all about which brands we import.
  endcomment
  unless product.tags contains 'Supplier Stock'
    comment
      OWN-STOCK TAG. This checked only 'Prince Tires', which 0 active products
      carry — the tag in use is 'Prince Stock' (355 products, measured
      2026-10-03), so own shelf stock was being quoted next-business-day
      instead of two hours. Both spellings accepted so a rename cannot silently
      break it again. Mirrored in src/lib/shopify/product-tier.ts — keep in sync.
    endcomment
    if product.tags contains 'Prince Stock' or product.tags contains 'Prince Tires'
      assign tier = 'A'
    endif

    for c in product.collections
      if c.handle == 'imported-tires'
        assign tier = 'A'
      endif
    endfor

    if tier == 'B'
      assign vendor_lower = product.vendor | default: '' | downcase
      for b in tierA_brands
        if vendor_lower contains b
          assign tier = 'A'
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endunless
-%}{{- tier -}}
